26
00:02:15.084 --> 00:02:15.937
Part 1.

27
00:02:16.217 --> 00:02:17.753
The System in One Page.

28
00:02:19.003 --> 00:02:20.433
What the platform must do.

29
00:02:20.713 --> 00:02:24.318
A ride-hailing platform is a real-time two-sided market.

30
00:02:24.598 --> 00:02:43.265
Every few seconds, in every neighbourhood, it must: see where riders want to go and where drivers are;. price each trip so riders accept and drivers are willing;. match riders to drivers so pickups are fast and the whole city stays efficient;. guide both to the pickup and the destination;. settle money correctly;.

31
00:02:44.615 --> 00:02:45.873
keep everyone safe.

32
00:02:46.153 --> 00:02:56.287
Mistakes are visible immediately: a 12-minute pickup, a surge that feels unfair, a driver sent across a flyover with no U-turn, an unpaid cash trip.

33
00:02:57.637 --> 00:02:58.725
