459
00:36:23.657 --> 00:36:31.358
Apache Flink computes per-cell supply and demand, segment speeds, surge inputs, fraud features and real-time dashboards;.

460
00:36:31.638 --> 00:36:36.481
Uber has described Flink-based platforms for real-time features (VERIFY).

461
00:36:37.831 --> 00:36:38.791
Lakehouse.

462
00:36:39.071 --> 00:36:46.580
Storage: all streams and CDC land in a lakehouse on distributed storage (HDFS or object storage);.

463
00:36:46.860 --> 00:36:57.271
Apache Hudi, created at Uber for incremental upserts on the lake (publicly described; VERIFY), handles late updates such as trip corrections and fare adjustments;.

464
00:36:57.551 --> 00:36:59.791
Iceberg or Delta are alternatives.

465
00:37:00.071 --> 00:37:01.415
Processing and query:

466
00:37:01.695 --> 00:37:09.503
Spark for batch; Presto or Trino for interactive SQL (Uber has described large Presto deployments; VERIFY).

467
00:37:10.853 --> 00:37:28.410
Models: facts: trips, requests (including unfulfilled), offers (accepted or declined or timeout), price quotes, payments, incentives, safety incidents, location aggregates;. dimensions: city, zone and cell (H3), driver, rider (pseudonymised), vehicle, product, time.

468
00:37:28.690 --> 00:37:31.677
Governance: location data is highly sensitive.

469
00:37:31.957 --> 00:37:40.405
Access is restricted by purpose, precise traces are retained only as long as needed, and aggregates are used for most analysis.

470
00:37:41.755 --> 00:37:42.992
Real-time OLAP.

471
00:37:43.272 --> 00:38:02.877
Apache Pinot, which Uber has described using heavily for real-time analytics (VERIFY), or ClickHouse or Druid, powers: city operations dashboards (requests, completion, ETAs per zone per minute);. surge monitoring;. driver earnings views;. restaurant or merchant dashboards in adjacent businesses.

472
00:38:04.227 --> 00:38:10.073
Why: a sub-second query over fresh data (seconds old) that the batch warehouse cannot provide.

473
00:38:11.423 --> 00:38:13.577
