474
00:38:13.857 --> 00:38:15.009
ML platform:

475
00:38:15.289 --> 00:38:22.543
Uber's publicly described Michelangelo covers feature management, training, deployment and monitoring (VERIFY).

476
00:38:22.823 --> 00:38:35.452
Reference: a feature store (offline in the lake, online in a low-latency store), training on Spark or GPUs, model registry, online serving with shadow and canary deployment, drift monitoring.

477
00:38:35.732 --> 00:38:36.521
Models:

478
00:38:36.801 --> 00:38:48.108
ETA correction, demand and supply forecasts, pricing elasticity, fraud, safety anomaly scoring, destination prediction, pickup point suggestion, support ticket routing.

479
00:38:48.388 --> 00:38:49.625
Experimentation:

480
00:38:50.975 --> 00:39:08.021
A or B tests randomised by user for UI changes;. switchback and geo-randomised designs for marketplace changes (pricing, matching, incentives), because riders and drivers interact;. a central platform computes metrics with variance reduction.

