552
00:42:03.859 --> 00:42:04.755
Part 9.

553
00:42:05.035 --> 00:42:07.851
Security, Privacy, Safety and Compliance.

554
00:42:09.101 --> 00:42:26.701
Location privacy: precise traces are restricted to purposes (trip, safety, disputes);. access is logged;. retention is limited, with aggregates for analytics;. riders see drivers' approximate positions before the trip and exact positions only during their trip.

555
00:42:28.051 --> 00:42:40.851
Personal data: masked phone numbers (a CPaaS proxy), minimal data shared between rider and driver, DPDP Act obligations in India (VERIFY) and GDPR where applicable.

556
00:42:41.131 --> 00:42:59.243
Aggregator regulation (India): licensing, driver verification, vehicle fitness, fare and surge rules, grievance redressal, safety features and data localisation provisions in the Motor Vehicle Aggregator Guidelines and state rules (VERIFY current texts; state rules vary).

557
00:42:59.523 --> 00:43:00.377
Payments:

558
00:43:00.657 --> 00:43:08.017
PCI scope reduction by tokenisation; RBI rules for card storage and payment aggregators (VERIFY).

559
00:43:09.367 --> 00:43:16.257
Safety data: incident data preserved and access-controlled; lawful process for law enforcement requests.

560
00:43:17.607 --> 00:43:18.461
Part 10.

561
00:43:18.741 --> 00:43:20.661
Reliability and Operations.

562
00:43:21.911 --> 00:43:30.636
City isolation: each city's marketplace runs in its own partitions, so a bad deploy or a runaway surge bug affects one city.

563
00:43:30.916 --> 00:43:34.457
Deploys roll out city by city (cells; Ch 34).

564
00:43:34.737 --> 00:43:49.201
Trips in progress must survive: the trip service is strongly consistent and replicated;. apps cache the trip state and continue navigation offline;. fare computation can happen after reconnection from buffered GPS.

565
00:43:49.481 --> 00:43:50.740
Degradation order:

566
00:43:52.090 --> 00:43:54.799
Heat maps and non-critical features go first.

567
00:43:55.079 --> 00:43:57.575
Then pooling, falling back to single rides.

568
00:43:57.855 --> 00:44:01.183
Then dynamic pricing falls back to a fixed multiplier.

569
00:44:01.463 --> 00:44:05.687
Matching falls back to greedy nearest-driver if the optimiser is slow.

570
00:44:05.967 --> 00:44:17.082
Multi-region: active-active across regions for stateless services; the trip store is replicated with failover; driver and rider connections reconnect to the healthy region.

571
00:44:18.432 --> 00:44:29.909
Observability: per-city dashboards of request, then match, then pickup, then complete funnel, ETA error, match latency, offer acceptance, payment success, and SOS response times.

572
00:44:30.189 --> 00:44:39.299
Peak events (New Year's Eve, cricket finals, festivals): forecasts feed pre-scaling and incentive plans, and operations teams are on standby.

573
00:44:40.649 --> 00:44:41.651
Part 11.

